# nl-startup-2: hung-core detection in the desktop (apply in apps/desktop/src/main/protocol/local-core.ts and the host that calls resolveLocalCore)
1. local-core.ts, function readCoreState: add to the returned object (and to its return type)
     controlPort: Number.isInteger(discovery.core?.control?.port) ? discovery.core.control.port : null,
     token: typeof discovery.endpoints?.session?.token === 'string' ? discovery.endpoints.session.token : null,
   (the parsed type gains core.control{port} and endpoints.session{token}).
2. After the app's core is launched (resolveLocalCore's onLaunched callback gives the child), start once per app run:
     const watcher = watchCore({
       readDiscovery: () => readCoreState(runtimeRoot),
       ownedPid: () => ownedCore?.pid ?? null,   // the child onLaunched last reported, null when it has exited
       log: (line) => logger.error(line),
     });
   import { watchCore } from '../../../../../packages/protocol-client/src/launch/ensure-core.mjs'; call watcher.stop() at quit
   (before coreExit). No onKilled is needed: the connection's reconnect ladder calls resolveLocalCore, whose ensureCore
   starts a replacement because the killed pid names no core.
